  "body": "Found by the second read of PR #3471 (comment 7081078749 on that PR). It is a reading of the code and of the usual control behaviour. It is NOT confirmed by a run, and no control ran it. The first step of the work is to confirm or to disprove it. If it is confirmed, this is wrong posted G-code and the priority goes to `P1`.\n\nPR #3471 stops a G2/G3 block whose written end point equals its written start point (#3442). One more case stays: only the radial axis word changes between the start and the end of an arc, and the written start is within half an output step of the line through the centre. Then the written start and the written end have the same angle about the centre. A control that reads an equal angle as a full turn can cut a spiral of nearly one full turn.\n\nBy reading, this needs a radius below about 0.05 mm with mm output (3 decimals), or about 0.3 mm with inch output (4 decimals).\n\n## Necessary work\n1. A recorded input with such an arc for the mm case and the inch case. Post it with `fanuc.cps` and `linuxcnc.cps`. Show the blocks.\n2. Find from public documentation of the two controls how each reads an arc whose start and end have the same angle and different radii.\n3. If the block is unsafe: extend the guard of `crates/post/src/post/arc_guard.rs` (for example, check the turn direction and the sweep from the WRITTEN words, and post a linear move when the written sweep is not the sweep of the record). Add the case to the table test over all posts.\n\nRefs #3442\n",
